   Two gates: PARITY (committed token-ids must EXACTLY match baseline — a value-changing edit is PARITY_FAIL) + PERF (adaptive-sampled decode-tok/s A/B; WIN iff f>=0.90 AND delta>FLOOR; DEAD if f<=0.65). The baseline is the SHARED fleet frontier: your variant is measured INCREMENTALLY against every worker's accumulated wins, and a WIN advances that shared baseline for everyone (so pick kernels others have not already improved this round). DEAD_FILE = you targeted a __global__ whose source is not compiled in (edit the base .hip that defines it); NO_OP = your variant was byte-identical to baseline. CROSS_ARCH = your gfx1201 win changes the compiled code of another fleet arch (gfx1100/gfx1151/gfx1030) — perf isolation is ABSOLUTE (-any% on another arch is unacceptable): wrap the gfx1201-specific part in `#if defined(__gfx1200__) || defined(__gfx1201__)` (or move it to a .gfx1201.hip variant) so other archs compile BYTE-IDENTICALLY, then re-submit. gfx12-only builtins (s_prefetch_data, wmma_*_gfx12, dot* w/ gfx12 feature) ALWAYS need this gate.
