**Learned:** Softpipe did **not** cut registers — compiler kept current+next live (`VGPR 72→88`). Occupancy and mem_busy rose, L2 fell, **tok/s flat**. Profile feedback: *“TLP already hides latency, NOT MLP-limited.”* So for qkvza, more MLP/schedule reordering is the wrong class; next rounds should try non-MLP levers (cheaper VALU/dual-issue or real cache policy), not another softpipe/prefetch variant.

