Clear DEAD: holding 8 weight headers exploded VGPR 96→248 and cut occupancy. Logging the result.## Round 1 complete

**Target:** `gemv_hfq4g256_moe_gate_up_k8_indexed` (12.8% wall, mem-active, L2 64.4%, occ ~52%, **vgpr 96**)

**Hypothesis:** Residual’s “weight MEMORY phase → pure FMA burst” win should help gate_up, which still interleaves `sc/zp/pk` loads with MACs inside `DOG_X8`. Sequential gate-then-up header loads for the whole group-quad, then the same FMA order.

**Lever:** `gup_w_mem_then_fma` — value-preserving (same math/slots; only live ranges / issue order change).

**Harness:** `DEAD` · **Δ −5.1%** · **f = 0.0** · 4 rounds · coherence OK

| | base | variant |
|---|---|---|
| decode tok/s (median) | 159.9 | 151.75 |
| VGPR | 96 | **248** |
| occ | 51.6% | **14.8%** |
| wall% | 12.5 | 16.1 |
| L2 hit | 64.3% | 89.4% |
| mem_busy | 53.7% | 58.5% |

**Learned:** Holding 8 full weight headers while 32-wide `x` is live blows the VGPR budget (96→248) and triggers **DROPPED-WAVES**. Gate_up is already register-tight with dual gate/up streams; residual-style `w_preload` is **closed** here. Higher L2 hit did not help once occupancy collapsed. Next levers should **cut** live state (or improve L2 without extending header live ranges), not batch more headers.

