+// reloads the same scale/zero header independently in all 32 lanes. On gfx12,
+// load those two immutable header words in lane 0 and broadcast their exact
+// bit patterns, retaining the original FMA/dequant order. This targets the
+// low mem_busy without changing any value or the non-gfx12 codegen.
