-// HFQ4-G256 GEMV with fused residual add: y[row] += A[row] · x.
-// Default (arch-agnostic) kernel. See gemv_hfq4g256.hip for the full
-// writeup on why this had to be re-ported from the gfx1100 variant to
-// produce byte-exact output against the MQ4 quality-gate baselines.
-// TL;DR: single-accumulator sequential summation drifts from the
-// 4-accumulator pairwise-combine ordering used to generate the
-// baselines on gfx1100, breaking cross-arch exactness.
-//
-// Identical math to gemv_hfq4g256 except the final write accumulates
-// into y instead of overwriting. Used for wo and w_down projections
-// in the Qwen3.5 forward path to eliminate one add_inplace_f32 launch
-// per residual (~10 µs per call).
-//
-// VARIANT R10c1 res_dequant_then_dot:
-// BOD residual: occ~23% mem_busy~45% L2~78% vgpr=72 — mixed, not
-// BW-saturated. Prior dual-row nibble-ILP (R5c1) was DEAD: compiler
-// already dual-issues independent dual-row DOG bodies. NEW lever:
-// split each DOG into (1) 8 independent dequant FMAs producing d0..d7
-// then (2) a pure 8-way dot with the hoisted x slice. Same FP ops as
-// baseline ((sc*n+zp)*x summed in the same left-to-right tree), but
-// dequant of all 8 nibbles is free of x-mul dependency so the
-// scheduler can dual-issue dequant across the nibble chain before the
-// x-dependent macs. Hypothesis: residual is VALU-latency-bound on the
-// fused dequant-mac chain (not MLP, not nibble-ILP across rows); this
-// lengthens the independent dequant wavefront without adding VGPR
-// pressure beyond 8 temps that should re-use the same physical regs.
-
