**Learned:** Wider header loads do not help residual. The compiler expanded live ranges (72→96 VGPR); TLP already covers header latency on this L2-resident dual-row GEMV. Header VMEM issue count is closed as a lever here — next residual work should avoid load-width / live-range growth and look for real VALU/dual-issue or structural changes.

