Running the certify harness for residual `res_inline_w`.codex
I found a distinct, untried lever: the initialization loop loads each row’s four Q8 state scales redundantly in all 32 lanes, while the scale address is warp-uniform. I’m instead testing a stronger but still exact variant on the same initialization path: on gfx1201 only, each group of four lanes performs one aligned 32-bit Q8 load and broadcasts the packed word, extracting the original signed bytes. It preserves every byte and every multiply, reduces byte-load issue pressure, and leaves non-gfx12 preprocessing identical.
