## Round 18 complete

**Target:** `gemv_hfq4g256_residual` (6.7% wall, 0/10 dead budget, ACTIVE)  
**BOD:** occ 22.5%, L2 77.6%, mem_busy 45.3%, VGPR 72 — L2-resident/mixed, high `valu_cyc`  
**Why this kernel:** High-wall EXHAUSTED kernels skipped; residual had open budget and a clear VGPR/live-x story after schedule levers (preload/chunk/unroll/ptrinc/sczp) all died with “TLP already hides latency.”

**Hypothesis (`res_lds_x_g256`):** Dual-row residual holds ~32 live x floats + 8 weight headers (VGPR 72). Stage each group’s 256×f32 x in 1KB LDS so peak x live drops to 8 floats; same `DOG_X8` product math and acc pairwise fold. Expect lower VGPR / higher occ.

**Harness:** `DEAD` — parity OK, **δ = −7.82%**, **f = 0.0** (4 rounds)

| Metric | before → after |
|--------|----------------|
| VGPR | 72 → **96** (went up) |
| occ | 22.5 → 34.9 |
| mem_busy | 45.3 → 66.8 |
| L2 hit | 77.6 → 85.4 |
| LDS | 0 → 1024 |
| wall% | 6.7 → **14.4** |

**Learned:** LDS x-stage is **not** residual’s bottleneck. The compiler expanded live ranges (VGPR 72→96) and barrier/LDS traffic inflated the kernel’s wall share; higher occ/mem_busy did not help because **TLP already hides latency**. Same failure mode as qkvza/down LDS-x — **closed for residual**.

