**Target:** `gemv_hfq4g256_residual` (6.7% wall, occ 22.5%, L2-resident/mixed, 1/10 dead — preferred over more-exhausted kernels; skipped all `[EXHAUSTED]` entries)

**Context:** A3B residual is K=2048 → 8 groups → 2 quads, tail=0. Prior K=2048 full-unroll raised VGPR 72→96 by holding both quads live.

**Hypothesis:** Sequential *scoped* quad bodies (nested braces for q=0 then q=1) would free q0 headers/x before q1, cut peak VGPR, and raise occupancy — same DOG math, gfx12-only path.

**Lever:** `res_k2048_scoped_seq`

