## Round 22 complete

**Target:** `gemv_hfq4g256_moe_down_k8_indexed_batched_expanded`  
(7.8% wall, 0 consecutive dead, L2-resident mixed: occ ~42.5%, mem_busy ~43.5%, VGPR 88)

**Hypothesis:** Full 8-header `w_preload` (R4c0) was DEAD. Per-DOG load+FMA is baseline. Middle ground: **group-phased MEMORY/FMA** — load 4 row headers for g0 → pure FMA → free them → same for g1. Peak header live = 4 (half of full preload), still batches VMEM vs VALU within each group.

**Result:** **DEAD** — parity OK, `f=0.625`, `delta_pct=+0.31%` (noise).

| Metric | Base (BOD) | Variant |
|--------|------------|---------|
| VGPR | 88 | 96 |
| occ | 42.5% | 41.9% |
| mem_busy | 43.5% | 43.2% |
| L2 hit | 75.8% | 71.8% |

**Learned:** Peak header live window is **not** the bottleneck. Compiler still raised VGPR; profile_feedback had no lever signal. Same TLP-hidden regime as full `w_preload` — both half- and full-header MEMORY/FMA batching are closed for this 4×2 down GEMV.

