Recording the DEAD result and writing the progress log line.## Round 37 complete

**Target:** `fused_rmsnorm_mq_rotate` (ACTIVE, fewest dead in digest, 4.6% wall, occ 0.1% catastrophic under-occ)

**Hypothesis:** Profile feedback keeps naming “per-wave MLP ring.” Prior levers changed permute ISA (`shfl_xor`) or soft-piped Phase-1a. I pipelined the 5 cross-lane FWHT stages: issue all 8 `ds_swizzle`s, then all 8 add/sub combines (same peer/polarity; gfx12-gated). Value-preserving, VGPR-neutral if temps die per stage.

**Harness:** `R37c0_rms_hbfly_swiz_pipe8` → **DEAD**  
- delta **+0.06%**, f=**0.50**, 4 rounds, parity OK  
- VGPR 48→48, occ stuck 0.2%  
- mem_busy 18.0→29.2%, L2 73.7→71.2%, wall 4.5→4.1% (kernel slice moved; decode did not)

**Learned:** Pipelining butterfly swizzles is not the limiter. This one-block kernel is launch-geometry bound (`grid=[1]`), not VALU-latency-bound inside HBFLY. Serial vs pipelined HBFLY issue order is closed; further in-kernel MLP on FWHT cross-lane stages is unlikely to move decode without host multi-block launch.

